IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`

-- Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA) -- interest and penalty tax (Part 5) and objections and appeals (Part 10),
-- as they bear on stamp duty. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms ("the taxpayer", "the
-- objector", "the Minister", "the Commissioner"). The individual's questions are in sda-seat.l4.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- through the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). The deposited text is AS AT 2019-10-03 (scraped 2024-09-13),
-- at ../../../taxation-administration-act-1996/registers/source-bundle/taxation-administration-act-1996.txt; the
-- Current Titles list of 22 September 2026 lists a version of 4.12.2025, so at least one later version is NOT
-- reflected here. Not the official text; may be out of date.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 25 (interest on a tax default, daily from the end of the last day for payment); s 26 (rate:
-- the market rate, an INPUT, plus 8% a year); s 27 (no interest under $20); s 29 (remission, a discretion); s 30
-- (penalty tax, and when it is not payable); s 31 (25% or 75%, adjusted for disclosure and obstruction); s 32 (no
-- penalty tax under $20); s 33 (penalty tax paid within the period in the assessment, regulative); s 82, s 86 (objection within
-- 60 days), s 87 (a late objection, up to 12 months, with the Minister's permission); s 89 (notice of the
-- determination); s 92 (right of appeal, including after 90 days without a determination), s 93 (50% of the tax paid
-- first), s 94 (appeal within 60 days, or at any time after 90 days undetermined with 14 days' notice), s 95 (a late
-- appeal, up to 12 months, at the Court's discretion).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: assessments and reassessments (Part 3) except as named, refunds (Part 4), special tax return
-- arrangements (Part 6), recovery (Part 7), records, investigations, secrecy and offences (Parts 8, 9), s 88
-- procedure, s 90 interest on refunds, and Supreme Court procedure.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1996 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Part 5 Division 1 -- interest (ss 25-27)`

-- s 26(1): "The interest rate that applies under this Division is the sum of -- (a) the market rate; and (b) 8 per cent
-- per annum." (2): the market rate is the average of the daily 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate for the May before the
-- financial year, or a rate the Minister gazettes -- not in the deposit, so an INPUT (a yearly figure).
`the premium over the market rate, per cent a year` MEANS 8

GIVEN `the market rate, per cent a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest rate under Part 5, per cent a year` MEANS
    `the market rate, per cent a year` PLUS `the premium over the market rate, per cent a year`

-- s 25(1): "If a tax default occurs, the taxpayer is liable to pay interest on the amount of tax unpaid calculated on a
-- daily basis from the end of the last day for payment until the day it is paid". READING (NOTES.md, finding 17): the
-- daily rate is the yearly rate divided by 365, and the rate is taken as constant over the period (it is fixed per
-- financial year, s 26(2)(a)). s 27: "If the amount of interest payable ... would ... be less than $20, no interest
-- is payable".
`the minimum interest (s 27)` MEANS 20

GIVEN `the tax unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the days unpaid after the last day for payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the market rate, per cent a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on a tax default` MEANS
    IF `raw interest` LESS THAN `the minimum interest (s 27)`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `raw interest`
    WHERE
        `raw interest` MEANS
            `the tax unpaid` TIMES (`the interest rate under Part 5, per cent a year` `the market rate, per cent a year` DIVIDED BY 100)
                TIMES `the days unpaid after the last day for payment` DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `Part 5 Division 2 -- penalty tax (ss 30-34)`

-- s 2 "deliberate tax default means a tax default that wholly or partly consists of or results from a deliberate act or
-- omission by the taxpayer or a person acting on behalf of the taxpayer". s 31(1): "(a) in the case of a deliberate tax
-- default -- 75 per cent of the amount of tax unpaid; or (b) in any other case -- 25 per cent".
DECLARE `Kind of tax default` IS ONE OF
    `a deliberate tax default`
    `a tax default that is not deliberate`

-- s 31(2): "(a) if the taxpayer made a sufficient disclosure of the tax default while not subject to a tax audit -- the
-- penalty tax is to be reduced by 80 per cent; (b) if the taxpayer made a sufficient disclosure ... while subject to a
-- tax audit -- ... reduced by 20 per cent; (c) if the taxpayer engaged in obstructive conduct while subject to a tax
-- audit -- the penalty tax may be increased by the Commissioner by 20 per cent." (c) is the Commissioner's to choose:
-- the answer is the most it may be.
DECLARE `Taxpayer conduct` IS ONE OF
    `no disclosure and no obstruction`
    `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit`
    `a sufficient disclosure while subject to a tax audit`
    `obstructive conduct while subject to a tax audit`

GIVEN `the default` IS A `Kind of tax default`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 31(1) penalty rate, per cent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the default`
    WHEN `a deliberate tax default` THEN 75
    WHEN `a tax default that is not deliberate` THEN 25

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Taxpayer conduct`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 31(2) adjustment, per cent of the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `no disclosure and no obstruction` THEN 100
    WHEN `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit` THEN 20
    WHEN `a sufficient disclosure while subject to a tax audit` THEN 80
    WHEN `obstructive conduct while subject to a tax audit` THEN 120

-- s 30(2): "Penalty tax is not payable in respect of a tax default if the Commissioner is satisfied that the tax default
-- was not a deliberate tax default and did not result, wholly or partly, from any failure by the taxpayer ... to take
-- reasonable care". s 32: "less than $20, no penalty tax is payable". s 34: the Commissioner may remit penalty tax "by
-- any amount" -- so this is the most that can be imposed, before any remission.
`the minimum penalty tax (s 32)` MEANS 20

GIVEN `the tax unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the default` IS A `Kind of tax default`
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it was not deliberate and reasonable care was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct` IS A `Taxpayer conduct`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty tax on a tax default` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner is satisfied it was not deliberate and reasonable care was taken`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `raw penalty` LESS THAN `the minimum penalty tax (s 32)`
         THEN 0
         ELSE `raw penalty`
    WHERE
        `raw penalty` MEANS
            `the tax unpaid` TIMES (`the s 31(1) penalty rate, per cent` `the default` DIVIDED BY 100)
                TIMES (`the s 31(2) adjustment, per cent of the penalty` `the conduct` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 33: "Penalty tax must be paid by a taxpayer within the period specified for that purpose in an assessment of the tax
-- liability of the taxpayer." The period is the assessment's (an INPUT, in days from service of the assessment). s 25(2):
-- interest under Division 1 "is payable ... in respect of a tax default that consists of a failure to pay penalty tax".
-- No penalty tax assessed (nil under s 30(2) or s 32, or remitted in full under s 34), no obligation.
GIVEN `penalty tax is assessed as payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days specified in the assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` IS
    IF `penalty tax is assessed as payable`
    THEN PARTY  `the taxpayer`
         MUST   `pay the penalty tax`
         WITHIN `the days specified in the assessment`
         HENCE  FULFILLED
         LEST   BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "TAA s 33: penalty tax must be paid within the period specified in the assessment; unpaid, it is a tax default on which interest runs daily (s 25(1), (2))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Part 10 Division 1 -- objections (ss 82, 86, 87, 89)`

-- s 82: "A person who is dissatisfied with -- (a) an assessment (other than a compromise assessment); or (b) a decision
-- under Part 4 concerning a refund ...; or (c) any other decision of the Commissioner under a taxation law that is not
-- declared to be a non-reviewable decision, may lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister."
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `an assessment of duty`
    `a compromise assessment`
    `a decision concerning a refund of duty`
    `another reviewable decision of the Commissioner`
    `a decision declared non-reviewable`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an objection may be lodged against` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a compromise assessment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a decision declared non-reviewable` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 86: "An objection must be lodged with the Minister not later than 60 days after -- (a) in the case of an objection to
-- an assessment -- the date of service of the assessment on the taxpayer; or (b) in the case of an objection to some
-- other decision -- the date on which the taxpayer was notified of the decision." s 87(1): the Minister "has a
-- discretion to permit a person to lodge an objection after the end of the 60-day period but not ... later than 12
-- months after" the same date (a non-reviewable decision, (3)).
`the days to object (s 86)` MEANS 60

GIVEN `the date of service or notification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object (s 86)` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to object (s 86)` `the date of service or notification`

GIVEN `the date of service or notification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day a late objection may be permitted (s 87)` MEANS
    `months after` 12 `the date of service or notification`

GIVEN `the date of service or notification` IS A DATE
      `the date the objection is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the Minister permits a late objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is lodged in time` IF
        `the date the objection is lodged` `is on or before` (`the last day to object (s 86)` `the date of service or notification`)
    OR  (    `the Minister permits a late objection`
         AND `the date the objection is lodged` `is on or before` (`the last day a late objection may be permitted (s 87)` `the date of service or notification`))

§§ `Part 10 Division 2 -- appeals (ss 92-95)`

-- s 93(1): "A taxpayer cannot exercise a right of appeal unless the taxpayer has paid to the Commissioner 50% of the
-- whole of the tax (not including interest and penalty tax under Part 5) to which the appeal relates as assessed".
-- (2): "the Minister has a discretion to permit the right of appeal to be exercised even though" it has not been paid.
GIVEN `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax to be paid before appealing (s 93)` MEANS
    `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the tax paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister permits the appeal without it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 93 payment condition is met` IF
        `the tax paid` AT LEAST `the tax to be paid before appealing (s 93)` `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax`
    OR  `the Minister permits the appeal without it`

-- s 94(1): "An appeal must be made by a person not later than 60 days after the date of service on the person of notice
-- of the Minister's determination of the person's objection." s 95: "The Supreme Court has a discretion to allow a
-- person to appeal after the end of the 60-day period but not ... later than 12 months after" that date.
`the days to appeal (s 94)` MEANS 60

GIVEN `the date of service of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal (s 94)` MEANS
    `days after` `the days to appeal (s 94)` `the date of service of the determination`

GIVEN `the date of service of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal (s 95)` MEANS
    `months after` 12 `the date of service of the determination`

-- s 92(b) and s 94(2): if "90 days (not including any period of suspension under section 88) have passed since the
-- person's objection was lodged with the Minister; and ... the Minister has not determined the objection and served
-- notice of the determination on the person, the person may appeal at any time provided that the Commissioner is given
-- not less than 14 days written notice of the person's intention to make the appeal."
`the days after which an undetermined objection may go to appeal (s 94(2))` MEANS 90
`the days of notice to the Commissioner (s 94(2))` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any s 88 suspension` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister has served notice of the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days since written notice of the intention to appeal was given to the Commissioner` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal may be made now on an undetermined objection (s 94(2))` IF
        `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any s 88 suspension` AT LEAST `the days after which an undetermined objection may go to appeal (s 94(2))`
    AND (NOT `the Minister has served notice of the determination`)
    AND `the days since written notice of the intention to appeal was given to the Commissioner` AT LEAST `the days of notice to the Commissioner (s 94(2))`

§§ `Part 10 -- objection and appeal (regulative)`

-- Clock: days from the date of service of the assessment (or notification of the decision). Objecting and appealing
-- are the person's choice, so not doing them is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED): an objection out of time is simply
-- not one the Minister must determine. s 89(1): "The Minister must give written notice to the objector of the
-- determination of the objection" -- no period is stated, so no WITHIN. The appeal period then runs from that notice.
-- `the days allowed to object` is 60 (s 86), or up to 12 months if the Minister permits (s 87).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
`the appeal after the determination (s 94(1))` MEANS
    PARTY `the objector`
    DO    `appeal to the Supreme Court`
    WITHIN `the days to appeal (s 94)`
    LEST  FULFILLED

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `the days allowed to object` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duty party` `Duty act`
DECIDE `Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` IS
    IF (NOT (`an objection may be lodged against` `the decision`))
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the objector`
         DO    `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister`
         WITHIN `the days allowed to object`
         HENCE (PARTY `the Minister`
                MUST  `give written notice of the determination of the objection`
                HENCE `the appeal after the determination (s 94(1))`)
         LEST  FULFILLED
